WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:04.037
 Matt, Ben, you've
been here before.

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:05.271
You know the deal.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.240
We're sending you
home to recreate

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:10.510
an iconic weapon from history.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.811
However, there's a twist.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:13.779
 Of course.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.180
 You knew there would be.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.517
Because you are both
"Forged in Fire" champions,

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:22.022
we have decided to bring back an
extremely challenging weapon--

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.261
the Scottish claymore.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:28.828
 Claymore!

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:29.729
Yay.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.231
WIL: Enjoy.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:34.166
This massive, two-handed
sword was wielded by Scottish

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:36.369
Highlanders as early as 1490.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.271
Made famous in
modern pop culture

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.674
by the film "Braveheart," its
impressive size and length

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.109
made it a fearsome weapon.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:46.312
The claymore is easily
recognizable by its quatrefoil,

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:48.414
crossguard, and angled arms.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.683
Due to its large size,
the heavy sword was

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:52.385
usually swung with two hands.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:55.321
It was so deadly it was
nicknamed the "slaughter-sword"

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.524
by the English who faced
it on the battlefield.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.325
Because of its
prowess, the claymore

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.728
was a mainstay of the Scottish
Army for nearly two centuries.

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:03.996
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.864
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:05.931 --> 00:01:06.598
 Good luck.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:07.767
 Good luck, man.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.737 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.976
 Today I plan to
get two billets

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.245
of Damascus welded
up, hopefully twisted,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.847
maybe welded to each other.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.549
It'll be a good day if I can get
all three of those things done.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.321
The big forge just
wasn't working right.

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.222
It was coughing and spitting.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:32.558
So I had to retire it
and just do everything

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:33.359
in the smaller forge.

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:38.197
It's tougher to work
with the smaller forge

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.733
because it's not as hot.

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:42.001
I'm five hours in.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.236
I haven't even gotten
the metal to start

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:46.639
making the sword yet, so.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.776
It's just one of those setbacks
that could really bite you.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.881 line:0%
 Plan today-- first
thing is to profile it,

00:01:54.981 --> 00:02:00.153 line:0%
grind it, get that thing into
heat treat as fast as possible.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.387
I just grind.

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:02.655
I'm grinding and
grinding and grinding,

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:06.358
and I'm trying to get
as much done as I can.

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:08.494
And then I run
into a major issue.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.397
[bleep]

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.798
Ugh!

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:17.069
There is a little thin spot that
I didn't mean to put in there.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.337
Just chasing it.

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:20.073
It's getting thinner
and thinner and thinner.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.008
Just gonna have to go with
it, though, because it's

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.543
not flexing weird there.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.078
It just looks weird.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.580
But when you're under a
time crunch and you rush,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.082
that's what happens.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:31.151
Let's just say I made
that traditionally thin.

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.320 line:0%
BEN: So it's the
beginning of day three.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.457
I finally got the
blade drawn out

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.659
and ready for the heat treat.

00:02:42.327 --> 00:02:43.996
This is the largest
quench I've ever done.

00:02:44.062 --> 00:02:45.330
It's making me quite nervous.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.266
I'm adding salt to make
sure it's the right height

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.601
when I put the sword in.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.637
My major concern with
the quench today, I

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.906
have to watch for warping
and any kind of twisting.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.408
You know, it's a
big, long blade.

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.911
A tiny little twist, and you
can almost corkscrew the thing.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.146
So I just have to
be really careful.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:03.650
[suspenseful music]

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.089
I'm very happy.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:11.190
The quench seemed
to go really well.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.591
Sword is still straight.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.326
It's a good day.

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:18.865 line:0%
MATT: So yesterday, I got
the sword rough assembled.

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:22.835 line:0%
I got the handle core fit
and the guard roughed out.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.004 line:0%
I'm feeling pretty confident
I'm gonna get done,

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.371 line:7%
and I am exhausted.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.441
There's two ways to become
rich as a knifemaker,

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.743
start with a small fortune
and start with a large one.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.114
And I'm not a rich person, so
$10,000 would definitely help.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:38.585
[music playing]

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.422
That was me.

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:45.491
So I suck cutting with
a two-handed sword.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.193
I think my sword is capable of
cutting much better than that.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.096 line:7%
We'll see what happens.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.297 line:7%
BEN: It's day five.

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:53.232 line:0%
At the end of last
night, I was very,

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:54.733 line:7%
very happy with my progress.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.803
Pulling the sword out of
the etch for the first time

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.337
was one of my favorite parts.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:01.674
I hose it down, and I get my
first glimpse of the pattern

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.843
that's in that blade.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.345
Absolutely gorgeous.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.413
And I've got a long list of
things that I need to do.

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:08.748
It's just time to get to work.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.586
I kind of feel like
a surrogate mother.

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:17.323
I spent an entire
week making this thing

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.726
and putting my blood,
sweat, and tears into it.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:24.997
But, uh, I think I
made something amazing.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.332
Can't imagine what
would be in it.

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:39.012
 Ben, Matt, welcome
to the gun range.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:41.747
 I'm thinking Ben is terrified
at the idea of somebody

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:42.882
shooting his sword.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.483
I was the first time,
too, so I understand.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.419
 As you can see,
we've brought back

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:51.357
a test worthy of a champion's
blade, bullet splitting.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.826
Each of your blades will
be locked into a vise that

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:56.962
will fire a single round at
your blades to test their edge

00:04:57.062 --> 00:04:58.931
retention and strength.

00:04:58.997 --> 00:05:02.435
Your weapons are strong, should
split the bullet no problem.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:07.806
They're not strong, well, your
blade could shatter entirely.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:08.441
Good luck.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.609
Matt, you're up first.

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:12.744
3, 2, 1.

00:05:12.811 --> 00:05:14.547
Engage.

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:15.281
[gunshot]

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:16.449
 [bleep] yeah!

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.250
 Nice.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.418
[gunshot]

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:24.123
 You got a couple little
dimples on the edge there.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.058
It's just a little
bit dulled, but

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:27.893
everything held up beautifully.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.727
Good job, Matt.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:29.595
MATT: Thank you.

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:30.729
 Ben, you're up.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:31.764
Are you ready?

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:32.832
 Sure.
Let's do it.

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:33.900
 You got it, man.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.168
J. NEILSON: Let's get it ready.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.604
 3, 2, 1.

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:40.573
Engage.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.474
[gunshot]

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:42.842
MATT: Nice.

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:44.010
BEN: There we go.

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:46.579 line:0%
 Yeah, that sucker
just fragmented.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:50.583
[gunshot]

00:05:57.656 --> 00:06:03.229
 Well, Ben, the only
problem I can see is, uh,

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:04.931
rubbed a little bit
of your etch off.

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.766
Did nothing at all to the blade.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.134
Edge is still perfect.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.468
BEN: Thank you.

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:11.570
 Gentlemen, the Scottish
claymore, as you know,

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.840
was a brutal weapon
on the battlefield.

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.175
So to test the sharpness
of your blades,

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:17.976
I'm gonna take a single
blow through both

00:06:18.043 --> 00:06:21.480
these front legs of the horse,
simulated with sugar cane.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:25.050
If your blades are sharp, they
should pass right through.

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.018
Matt, you're up.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:26.818
Are you ready?

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:27.353
 Yeah.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.186
Kill the horse.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:31.057
[dramatic music]

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:39.265
 Matt, this weapon
is so amazingly light

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:44.303
and flexible, as well, that when
I hit, there was no resistance.

00:06:44.369 --> 00:06:46.205
It literally passed
right through the legs.

00:06:46.271 --> 00:06:47.973
I was through them
before I knew it.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:48.775
Well done, Matt.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.208
Really well done.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:51.243
Ben, you ready?

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.044
 Let's do it.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:52.945
DAVID: All right.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:53.812
Let's give it a try.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:57.483
[dramatic music]

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:05.224
 He's still down.

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:06.625
 Yeah.

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:08.961
 Well, Ben, it cut cleanly
through the first leg.

00:07:09.027 --> 00:07:11.930
Kind of bogged down on the
second leg, unlike Matt's.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:14.600
And I have a feeling it's
the width of the profile

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.504
up here just slowing
it down a bit.

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:21.474
But I don't think that
horse is running ever again.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.408
Nicely done, Ben.

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:23.709
 Thank you.

00:07:23.775 --> 00:07:26.946
 Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:30.783
To see how lethal on your blades
are, I will take your claymore,

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:33.251
and I will try to cut
through these pig carcasses

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:34.620
with one chop.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.089
As you know, last
season, both claymores

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:40.959
suffered catastrophic
failures on this very test.

00:07:41.059 --> 00:07:44.296
Let's see how much lethal
damage your blades can do.

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.130
Matt, you're up first.

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:45.997
Are you ready?

00:07:46.064 --> 00:07:46.866
 Go for it.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:47.767
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:50.102
[music playing]

00:07:56.441 --> 00:07:57.008
 It didn't break.

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:57.844
That's a win.

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:03.649
 Matt, I love the
feel of your blade.

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.018
It feels very
comfortable in the hands.

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.586
It's very easy to maneuver.

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:09.822
It was sharp enough
to cut through,

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:13.458
in terms of lacerating,
but it's just so flexible,

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:15.361
it didn't go through.

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:20.799
For this test, sir,
it will not kill.

00:08:20.899 --> 00:08:23.335
 I'm pissed at
that pig right now.

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:24.169
 Ben, you're up next.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:24.937
Are you ready?

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:26.105
 Hope so.

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:27.038
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:28.975
[dramatic music]

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.082
 [exhales]

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:37.249
 Ben, this blade
just sliced all

00:08:37.349 --> 00:08:39.317
the way through that carcass.

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:41.253
It's flexible.

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:43.923
It's got good feel to the cut.

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.325
This, sir, will kill.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:47.459
 Thanks.

00:08:47.526 --> 00:08:49.361
DOUG: Good job, man.

00:08:49.428 --> 00:08:51.530
 Matt, Ben, welcome back.

00:08:51.596 --> 00:08:53.432
The judges have
evaluated your weapons'

00:08:53.498 --> 00:08:55.768
performance and construction.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.404
It was difficult, but they've
made their final decision.

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:02.074
Gentlemen, both of your weapons
are bulletproof, they're sharp,

00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:03.609
and they're deadly.

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:06.045
But today, there can only be
one "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:09.282
[dramatic music]

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:14.554
Ben, congratulations.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:18.123
You are our first two-time
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.491
Great job.

00:09:19.591 --> 00:09:21.126
Matt, I have to ask
you to surrender

00:09:21.193 --> 00:09:22.761
your Scottish claymore.

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:25.097
 I'm a "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:26.432
That's never gonna go away.

00:09:26.498 --> 00:09:27.766
I don't feel like
I failed in this.

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.768
I don't feel like I'm a
loser in this or anything.

00:09:29.835 --> 00:09:32.538
I just feel like Ben
did slightly better.

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:34.773
And that's awesome.

00:09:34.873 --> 00:09:40.145
 Ben, you are our first and
only two-time "Forged in Fire"

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:41.514
champion.

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.349
You will also be receiving
that check for $10,000.

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:46.852
 Your claymore is a thing of
beauty, not only to look at,

00:09:46.953 --> 00:09:48.086
but to wield.

00:09:48.153 --> 00:09:49.055
[clapping]

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:50.989
- I'm at a loss for words.
- Thank you.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:51.857
DOUG: Great job.

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:53.058
 Oh, my God.

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:56.128
I am the "Forged in Fire"
champion of champions.

00:09:56.195 --> 00:09:57.496
I can't believe it.

00:09:57.563 --> 00:09:59.565
The people I was competing
against are so good.

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:02.034
To actually have come
out and win this thing,

00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:03.401
it's absolutely amazing.

00:10:03.502 --> 00:10:06.672
[music playing]

